# Repository boundary
#
# Keep in Git:
# - source code, tests, configuration, and automation
# - experiment notebooks and their lightweight records (README, result, metrics,
#   SESSION_NOTES, and steering documents)
# - documentation, survey notes, and the submission history Markdown
# - one-off analysis code and raw lightweight outputs under studies/, and
#   completed analysis reports under docs/surveys/
#
# Keep out of Git:
# - credentials and machine-local settings
# - raw/derived competition data and local Python environments
# - copied Kaggle upload packages, downloaded Kaggle outputs, feature caches,
#   model weights, and generated prediction/submission files in the output
#   locations ignored below
#
# Standard cache and credential rules below still apply inside tracked
# directories (for example, studies/__pycache__/ remains ignored).

# Python environments and caches
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.venv/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Local agent/editor state
/.codex/
/.cache/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Environment files and credentials
.env
.env.*
/.kaggle/
/.badge-collector/
kaggle.json
credentials.json
token.json
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx

# Competition data and local/external tools
/data/raw/
/data/processed/
/data/external/
/tools/*
!/tools/README.md

# Per-experiment generated or copied directories. Keep directory sentinels so a
# freshly cloned current-format experiment still passes structural validation.
/experiments/*/artifacts/*
!/experiments/*/artifacts/.gitkeep
/experiments/*/submission/
/experiments/*/kaggle/
/submission.csv
/experiments/*/submission.csv

# Legacy generated-output locations. New outputs belong under artifacts/.
/experiments/*/features/
/experiments/*/variants/

# One-off analysis tables and figures belong under studies/.
/artifacts/

# Generated model and array/table formats
*.ckpt
*.pth
*.pt
*.onnx
*.pkl
*.joblib
*.parquet
*.feather
*.npy
*.npz

# Notebook runtime state
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# OS/editor
.DS_Store
